            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for a hint, then the Hindi for to charm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ज़ाहिर",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ज़ाहिर — zāhir — \"evident, plain\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ज़ाहिर है कि अगर तुम सोओगे नहीं तो थक जाओगे। zāhir hai ki agar tum sooge nahīṃ to thak jāoge. It's plain that if you don't sleep, you'll get tired."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ज़ाहिर (zāhir) is usually traced to Arabic ẓāhir, \"outward, apparent\", which reached Hindi through Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
